senses.gloss:
Sthūṇa, or ˚na, m.
(1) also Sthūnā (dental n), f. (= Pali Thūṇa), n. of a brahman-village in the west: Mvy 〔4117〕 sthūṇopasthūṇau grāmau; Divy 〔22.1〕 (paścimena) Sthūṇopasthūṇakau brāhmaṇagrāmakau; Māy 〔1, 60〕 Sthūnāyāṃ, loc.;
(2) n. of a yakṣa at Sthūnā: Māy 〔60〕. [] (Pali does not record an equivalent of Upasthūṇa, q.v.)
